One approach I can think of is to add the following field to UpdateServiceMapResult:
```
	NoHealthCheck map[types.NamespacedName]bool
```
It would be filled in UpdateServiceMap() this way
```
		if info.HealthCheckNodePort() != 0 {
			result.HCServiceNodePorts[svcPortName.NamespacedName] = uint16(info.HealthCheckNodePort())
		} else {
			result.NoHealthCheck[svcPortName.NamespacedName] = true
		}
```
This new map would be passed to SyncEndpoints() so that we can skip logging by checking this map:
```
		if hcs.services[nsn] == nil {
			if !NoHealthCheck[nsn] {
				klog.V(3).Infof("Not saving endpoints for unknown healthcheck %q", nsn.String())
			}
```

I have a patch along the above line.
@danwinship 
If it is good by you, I can send a PR.
